# Links

The grammar colours a link that stands alone on a line. A link inside a
sentence or a list item gets its colour from the language server, when the
server runs.

## Alone on a line

[[catalog]]

[[catalog|the catalog]]

[[cells#a-table]]

[[cells#a-table|the table]]

![[catalog]]

## Inside a sentence

The cells read [[catalog]], and [[cells#a-table|the table]] shows the result.

## In a list

- [[python]], which the editor colours
- [[kotlin]], which needs an extension
- [[hql|HQL]], which this extension colours

## A link to no card

[[no-such-card]]

A sentence with [[no-such-card]] in it.

## A block anchor

This paragraph has an anchor. ^first-anchor

[[links#^first-anchor]]
